README

This repository contains all source data and code for the manuscript titled: 
“Comparative analysis of centromeres of oat (Avena sativa) and its tetraploid and diploid relatives reveals rapid evolution of centromere composition and architecture”.

Directories are named after the figures to which they contain relevant data and code. In cases where further explanation is required additional READMEs are included.


-------------> Subset of TREP database + new consensus
contains:
A Poaceae specific subset of the TREP database including newly produced consensus sequences

POA_TEdb_subset_TREP


-------------> TE sequence fasta datasets 

TE_consensus_sequences contains:
Consensus sequences in fasta format for the individual TE subfamilies described in the paper

TEpop_RLG_Aurora_flat
TEpop_RLG_Ava_flat
TEpop_RLG_Beth_flat
TEpop_RLG_Cereba_flat

These files contain:
Full collection of full-length TE copies identified with the TEpop pipeline in fasta format
The description line contains:
- Full name of the individual TE copy (contains chromosome name)
- Start and end position on the respective chromosome
- Transcriptional orientation (F/R)
- Sequence of the target site duplication (TSD, usually 5 identical bp flanking the TE, but can contain mismatches)
- Subfamily designation
